{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it was after the plague.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, commanded to count Israel to make them known that they would wage war against the Canaanites. And they were counted twice, and this counting counted to mention the names of the families, but in the wilderness of Sinai the families were not mentioned. And according to the plain sense, not all the sons of the tribes went up to families, for some of them had no children and were called by the name of their brothers, whose family was numerous, and they were absorbed among them and had no name of their own. For example, the children of Simeon — he does not count the families of Ohad, Jachin, and Zohar. And also the children of Asher — he did not count the family of Ishuah, and it was absorbed into the family of Ishvi. And sometimes a family is called only by the name of their grandsons, for example: לזרח משפחת הזרחי — and we do not find Zerah among the sons of Simeon, but he was among his grandsons, and the family was hung upon him. And likewise Ezbon, and likewise Ard and Naaman, who are the sons of Bela — from the fact that it says משפחת הבלעי, by implication Bela had other sons, and they were called by his name. And likewise Gilead made a family for himself, and Machir had other sons, and they were called by his name, as it is written: למכיר משפחת המכירי. And some of them had the ends of their names changed, for example: Nemuel, Yemuel, Hushim, Soham — the brothers of Ahiram; Mupham, Shupham."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:24.819306392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}